y be very careful when you're  downloading apps  on your mobile phones you still have a  certain level of security where you can  go to the apple marketplace or the  google play store  and they do have some level of control  but when you talk about windows  operating systems you're going to open  the internet to look for different kinds  of software  you have no idea whether the website  that you're on is trustworthy or is  hosted by a hacker with a malware on  that particular file that you're  downloading  especially if you're downloading a  pirated program never download a pirated  program  when you're downloading an executable  file you can upload it to virustotal.exe  scan  it to see if there are any viruses or  malware within it  the website also helps you analyze urls  to see if the url itself may have any  malicious attacks within them  so you can use that website to scan the  apps that you're downloading and see if  there's anything malicious about  those apps so that was all about our  cyber security training for this session  before wrapping up this session i'd like  to address a few questions from you  viewers  i can see that we have a few repeatedly  asked questions from our viewers  let me address a couple of those  questions  the first question that i'm taking up is  i want to start a career in cyber  security what steps should i take  well there is no one genuine path to  working in cyber security  you should have a bachelor's degree in  any relevant field and have a deep  abiding interest to know how cyber  security works  you must also possess a relevant job  experience preferably in the field of  i.t  you should have knowledge of network  configuration tcp  network protocols firewalls vpns and  operating systems  apart from these you need to know the  secure coding practices  threat modeling virtualization  technologies  encryption technologies date and  database management systems  after you're well versed with these  skills go for a few certifica